# Line endings are LF everywhere, on every platform.
#
# This is not cosmetic. The plugin ships as a hand-authored bundle that the DSH
# client evaluates as-is, and the published tarball is what users install — if a
# Windows checkout rewrote the bundle to CRLF while a Linux checkout did not, the
# artifact would differ per contributor, and a gate that reads the bundle as text
# (check/registration both do) could pass in one checkout and fail in another.
# Pinning `eol=lf` makes the committed bytes the same for everyone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch these: a rewritten PNG is a corrupt PNG, and the shell/command
# shims some tools ship must keep their own endings.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.gif binary
*.jpg binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Generated, but reviewed like source: keep diffs line-by-line.
tools/TEST-REPORT.md text eol=lf
